jobs.prompt:
Acceptance review (read-only; do not edit any file except the one result file named below) of tickets built on branch swarm/s2-build-owns-tests. For each ticket below, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met by the implementation, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read the files; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-0040", "title": "Make build tickets own their test files in ticket-manifest prompts", "files": ["tools/ticket-manifest.mjs"], "acceptance": ["A build ticket writes or owns the test file that proves it, so there is no build \u2192 test \u2192 fix chain.", "The critical path of a typical scope is shorter than before on the same input."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0041", "title": "Keep test tickets after build modules in wiring order", "files": ["tools/wiring.mjs"], "acceptance": ["orderTestsAfterBuild leaves build tickets that list tests without waiting on separate test tickets.", "A split ingest note is emitted when test ordering is flipped."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0042", "title": "Wire build-owns-tests rules into scope split ingest", "files": ["tools/scope-commands.mjs"], "acceptance": ["scope split --ingest accepts a build ticket that lists tests in its tests field without a separate test ticket.", "The ingest report shows a shorter dependency chain than test-first splits."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-s2-build-owns-tests.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test. Be strict and concrete.
